<title>ITALY: ATHLETICS-TERGAT WINS THIRD TITLE IN THRILLING DUEL.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-TERGAT WINS THIRD TITLE IN THRILLING DUEL.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenya's Paul Tergat won his third consecutive senior men's world cross country title on Sunday.</p>
<p>Tergat had a thrilling duel over the final two kilometres of the 12.333 km race with Morocco's Salah Hissou before pulling away with the line in sight.</p>
<p>Tergat won in 35 minutes 11 seconds with Hissou second and Kenya's Thomas Nyariki third.</p>
</text>
